<div class="wrap prose">
  <div class="eyebrow eyebrow-red">Policies</div>
  <h1>Health and safety policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Roofing means working at height, so safety comes before speed on every job. This statement sets out how {{ site.name }} keeps customers, the public and the people doing the work safe.</p>
  <p class="updated">Last updated 10 November 2026 · reviewed every year</p>

  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>{{ site.name }} is a trading name of {{ site.ownerFullName }}, a sole trader roofer. We will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Comply with the Health and Safety at Work etc. Act 1974, the Work at Height Regulations 2005, the Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2015 and all other law that applies.</li>
    <li>Plan every job so the risks are identified and controlled before work starts.</li>
    <li>Protect customers, neighbours and the public as well as ourselves.</li>
    <li>Use suitable, well-maintained equipment and the right protective clothing.</li>
    <li>Stop work if it can't be done safely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before work starts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every job gets a risk assessment, and a method statement for the way the work will be done. Customers and contractors can have a copy on request.</li>
    <li>We agree with the customer how access, parking, deliveries and their own movements around the property will work.</li>
    <li>We check for overhead power lines, fragile roof surfaces, roof lights and, in older buildings, materials that may contain asbestos.</li>
    <li>Weather is checked before and during work. We don't work on roofs in high winds, ice or heavy rain.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Working at height</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Edge protection, scaffolding or mobile towers are used wherever the job needs them. Scaffolding is put up by qualified scaffolders.</li>
    <li>Ladders are only used for short-duration access or light work. They are secured, inspected before use, and of the right class.</li>
    <li>Fragile surfaces, such as roof lights and old sheeting, are never walked on. They are covered or fenced off.</li>
    <li>Tools and materials are kept secure on the roof so nothing can fall, and the area below is fenced off or kept clear.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Equipment and protective clothing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Access equipment and harnesses are inspected before use and regularly checked, with defective items taken out of use.</li>
    <li>Hard hats, gloves, eye and hearing protection, dust masks and safety boots are worn where the work needs them.</li>
    <li>Power tools are kept in good condition and used with the right guards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hazardous materials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't remove or disturb asbestos. If we suspect it, work stops and a licensed specialist is called in.</li>
    <li>Resins, adhesives, solvents and fuels are stored, used and disposed of following the makers' safety data sheets.</li>
    <li>Dust from cutting slate and tile is controlled by wet cutting or extraction, and with suitable masks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Customers and the public</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The work area is clearly marked, and kept tidy and free of trip hazards.</li>
    <li>Ladders and access equipment are never left where children or the public could climb them.</li>
    <li>Sites are left safe and secure at the end of each day.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Accidents and first aid</h2>
  <p>A first-aid kit is kept in the van. Any accident or near miss is recorded, and reported under RIDDOR where the law requires, and we learn from it to stop it happening again.</p>

  <h2>Insurance and training</h2>
  <p>We hold public liability insurance and can send a copy of the certificate on request. We keep our training and knowledge of safe working practice up to date.</p>

  <h2>Subcontractors</h2>
  <p>Anyone working with us must work to this policy, hold suitable insurance and be competent for the work they do.</p>

  <h2>Responsibility</h2>
  <p>{{ site.ownerFullName }} is responsible for health and safety on all our work. Questions or concerns: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> or <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneLink }}">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>.</p>
